---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const effective = "July 29, 2026";
const updated = "July 29, 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | LPR Business Services"
  description="How LPR Business Services collects, uses, and protects information on lapiedraroja.com. We keep our data practices narrow and do not sell your information."
>
  <!-- header -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-white to-cream/40 border-b border-line">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] tracking-[0.16em] uppercase text-red-bright">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl mt-3 leading-[1.1]">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-graytext mt-4">Effective {effective} · Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 text-graytext leading-relaxed text-[17px]">
    <p class="text-ink text-lg">
      This Privacy Policy explains how Danielle Stone, doing business as LPR Business Services
      (“LPR Business Services,” “we,” “us,” or “our”), collects, uses, and protects information when
      you visit <a class="text-red-deep hover:underline" href={site.domain}>lapiedraroja.com</a>
      (the “Site”) or contact us through it. We keep our data practices deliberately narrow: we
      collect only what we need to respond to you and to keep the Site running securely, and we do
      not sell your information.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">1. Who we are</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      LPR Business Services provides bookkeeping, accounting, controller, and CFO-level advisory
      services. This Site is our marketing website. For any question about this Policy or your
      information, use the contact details in <a class="text-red-deep hover:underline" href="#contact">Section 12</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">2. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-display text-ink mt-6">Information you give us</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      When you submit our contact form, we collect your <strong class="text-ink">name</strong>,
      <strong class="text-ink">email address</strong>, and <strong class="text-ink">the message you
      write</strong> (all required), and, if you choose to provide them, your
      <strong class="text-ink">business name</strong> and <strong class="text-ink">industry</strong>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you email or call us directly, we receive whatever information you include in that
      communication. Please do not send sensitive personal or financial details (such as account
      numbers or tax identifiers) through the Site’s contact form or by unencrypted email.
    </p>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-display text-ink mt-6">Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      When you visit the Site, our hosting provider records standard technical information for
      security and reliability, such as your IP address, browser type, device type, and the pages you
      request. We also use a <strong class="text-ink">privacy-first, cookieless web analytics tool</strong>
      that measures Site traffic in aggregate (for example, which pages are most visited). This tool
      does not use cookies, does not track you across other websites, and does not build an
      advertising profile of you.
    </p>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-display text-ink mt-6">Cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do <strong class="text-ink">not</strong> use advertising, marketing, or cross-site tracking
      cookies. Our hosting and security provider may set a small number of strictly necessary cookies
      to protect the Site from abuse and keep it functioning. You can block or delete cookies in your
      browser settings; the Site will continue to work normally.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">3. How we use your information</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">We use the information above only to:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
      <li>respond to your inquiry and communicate with you about our services;</li>
      <li>provide, operate, and improve the Site;</li>
      <li>keep the Site secure and prevent fraud or abuse;</li>
      <li>understand, in aggregate, how the Site is used; and</li>
      <li>comply with our legal, tax, and accounting obligations.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We do not use your information for automated decision-making that has a legal or similarly
      significant effect on you, and we do not use it for targeted advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">4. How we share your information</h2>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-cream p-5 mt-4">
      <p class="text-ink font-medium">
        We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioral
        advertising.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4">We share information only in these limited circumstances:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Service providers</strong> that help us run the Site and respond to
        you, including our website hosting and analytics provider, our contact-form and
        workflow-automation provider, and our email provider. These providers process information
        only on our behalf and only as needed to perform their service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Legal requirements</strong>, if required by law, subpoena, or court
        order, or to protect our rights, safety, or property, or that of others.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-ink">Business transfer</strong>, if the business is ever sold or
        reorganized, in which case information may transfer as part of that transaction; we would
        notify you first.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">5. Data security</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Site is served over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection, and we limit access to the information
      we receive to authorized personnel. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure,
      so while we use reasonable safeguards, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">6. Data retention</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We keep contact-form submissions and related correspondence only as long as needed to respond
      to you and to maintain a record of our business communications, and thereafter as required for
      legal, tax, or accounting purposes. When information is no longer needed, we securely delete it.
      Aggregate analytics data does not identify you individually.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">7. Your privacy rights</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of the following rights regarding your
      personal information: to <strong class="text-ink">access</strong> the information we hold about
      you, to request <strong class="text-ink">correction</strong> of inaccurate information, to
      request <strong class="text-ink">deletion</strong>, and to
      <strong class="text-ink">object to</strong> or restrict certain uses. To exercise any right,
      contact us using <a class="text-red-deep hover:underline" href="#contact">Section 12</a>. We
      will respond within the time required by applicable law and may need to verify your identity
      first. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.
    </p>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-display text-ink mt-6">California residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what personal information we
      collect and how we use it (described in this Policy), the right to request access to or deletion
      of that information, and the right to correct it.
      <strong class="text-ink">We do not sell or share personal information</strong> as those terms
      are defined under California law, and we do not use or disclose sensitive personal information
      beyond what is needed to provide our services.
    </p>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-display text-ink mt-6">Canadian residents (PIPEDA)</h3>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you are in Canada, you may request access to the personal information we hold about you and
      ask us to correct it. We collect and use personal information only for the purposes described in
      this Policy and with your consent, which you may withdraw at any time.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">8. Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Site is intended for businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information
      from children under 16. If you believe a child has provided us information, please contact us
      and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">9. Links to other sites</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Site may link to third-party websites (such as our LinkedIn page). We are not responsible
      for the privacy practices of those sites, and we encourage you to review their privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">10. Changes to this Policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We may update this Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the “Last updated” date
      above and post the new version on this page. We encourage you to review it periodically.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl mt-12">11. Reaching a supervisory authority</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you have a concern we cannot resolve, California residents may contact the California Privacy
      Protection Agency or California Attorney General, and Canadian residents may contact the Office
      of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact" class="text-2xl mt-12">12. Contact us</h2>
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-cream p-6 mt-4">
      <p class="text-ink font-medium">Danielle Stone · LPR Business Services</p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Email: <a class="text-red-deep hover:underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a class="text-red-deep hover:underline" href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
